  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, ordinary day 15 January 1929; the four retiring Unionist councillors were again nominated and returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 7 January 1929, p. 11). 'The four retiring Unionist councillors were again nominated for the corresponding vacancies. They are Messrs. Thomas Gibson, J.P. (chairman of the Council), Hugh Elliott, George Faulkner, and Joseph I. Thompson. There will be no contest.' Returned unopposed."
